@startuml
title "As a Buyer, I want to use the Web UI to list items on sale of a given publisher (direct sales and auctions)." - Process_View_SD

skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Futura
skinparam objectFontSize 20
skinparam backgroundColor CornSilk
skinparam objectBackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFE0
skinparam ArrowFontColor #3B4953
skinparam ActivationBackgroundColor black
hidefootbox
autonumber

actor "Buyer" as Buyer
participant ":Frontend" as Frontend
participant ":Backend" as Backend
database ":Database" as db

Buyer -> Frontend : Opens marketplace
activate Frontend

Frontend -> Backend : OPTIONS /api?email={email}
activate Backend
Backend --> Frontend : 200 OK%n()Root links
deactivate Backend

' --- Fetch Direct Sales ---
Frontend -> Frontend : activeSalesHref = links["active-direct-sales"].href
Frontend -> Backend : getByHref(activeSalesHref)
activate Backend
Backend -> db : find active direct sale listings
activate db
db --> Backend : active sales data
deactivate db
Backend --> Frontend : 200 OK%n()CollectionModel (Direct Sales)
deactivate Backend

' --- Fetch Auctions ---
Frontend -> Frontend : auctionsHref = links["auctions"].href
Frontend -> Backend : getByHref(auctionsHref)
activate Backend
Backend -> db : find active auction listings
activate db
db --> Backend : active auctions data
deactivate db
Backend --> Frontend : 200 OK%n()List<AuctionResponseDTO>
deactivate Backend

Frontend -> Frontend : Cache items and derive unique publisher options in memory
Frontend --> Buyer : Displays marketplace items (Sales & Auctions)

Buyer -> Frontend : Selects Publisher MultiSelect filter
Frontend -> Frontend : Filter cached sales and auctions locally by publisher
Frontend --> Buyer : Displays matching active sales and auctions
deactivate Frontend

note over Frontend, Backend
The publisher filter is applied locally to both cached collections in memory.
The Frontend does not perform new network requests when toggling publisher criteria.
end note

@enduml